      <div type="clause" n="12">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:ICn">I Cn</ref> 12</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="12" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="294" ed="#liebermann"/>And leohtgesceot þriwa on geare<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#ICn_12.lnote.oe.9"/>: ærest on Easteræfen healfpenigwurð<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#ICn_12.lnote.oe.10"/> wexes æt ælcere<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#ICn_12.lnote.oe.11"/> híde ⁊ eft on<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="12" target="#ICn_12.lnote.oe.12"/> Ealra halgena mæssan eallswa<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="13" target="#ICn_12.lnote.oe.13"/> mycel [⁊<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="**" target="#ICn_12.lnote.oe.star2"/> eft to þæm<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="14" target="#ICn_12.lnote.oe.14"/> sanctan Marian clænsunge ealswa].</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="12" corresp="#wit-a"><pb n="294" ed="#liebermann"/>And leohtgesceot þriwa on geara: arest on Easteræfen healfpeningwurð wexes æt ælcere hide ⁊ eft to Ealra halgena mæssan ealswa mycel.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="12" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="294" ed="#liebermann"/>Et<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#ICn_12.lnote.oe.6"/> fiat ter in anno simbolum luminis: primum in uigilia Pasche obolata<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#ICn_12.lnote.oe.7"/> cerę de omni hida (car<hi rend="italic">ruca<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#ICn_12.lnote.oe.8"/></hi>); in festo Omnium sanctorum tantundem<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#ICn_12.lnote.oe.9-2"/>, tertio tantundem in festo sancte Marię candelarum.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="12" corresp="#wit-inst-cn"><pb n="295" ed="#liebermann"/>. . . .<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#ICn_12.lnote.oe.11-2"/> Scotum ad luminaria, quod Angli uocant lihtgescot<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="12" target="#ICn_12.lnote.oe.12-2"/>, ter in anno (uno<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="13" target="#ICn_12.lnote.oe.13-2"/>) detur de unaquaque hyda (id<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="14" target="#ICn_12.lnote.oe.14-2"/> est suling): cera unius oboli in uigilia Paschę, in uigilia Sanctę Marię (in<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="15" target="#ICn_12.lnote.oe.15"/> mense Augusto), <ptr type="liebermannNote" n="16" target="#ICn_12.lnote.oe.16"/>in uigilia Omnium sanctorum . . . .<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="17" target="#ICn_12.lnote.oe.17"/></ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="12" corresp="#wit-cons-cn"><pb n="295" ed="#liebermann"/>Et census luminaris ter in anno: primum in uigilia Pasche obolata cere ab omni hida et iterum in festiuitate Omnium sanctorum tantumdem et tertio in Purificacione sancte Marie tantumdem.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="12" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="164" ed="#robertson"/>And leohtgesceot þriwa on geare: ærest on Easteræfen healfpenigwurð wexes æt ælcere híde ⁊ eft on<ptr type="editorNote" n="9" target="#ICn_12.robnote.fn.9"/> Ealra halgena mæssan eallswa mycel [⁊ eft<ptr type="editorNote" n="10" target="#ICn_12.robnote.fn.10"/> to þæm (æfene)<ptr type="editorNote" n="11" target="#ICn_12.robnote.fn.11"/> sanctan Marian clænsunge ealswa].</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="244" ed="#rabin-doml"/>And leohtgesceot þriwa on geare: ærest on Easteræfen healfpenigwurð wexes æt ælcere hide and eft on Ealra Halgena mæssan eallswa mycel, and eft to þæm æfene Sanctan Marian clænsunge ealswa.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="295" ed="#liebermann"/>Und Lichtschoss dreimal im Jahre: von jeder Hufe<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#ICn_12.lnote.de.1"/> einen Halbpfennigwerth<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#ICn_12.lnote.de.2"/> an Wachs zuerst am Ostervorabend und wieder am<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#ICn_12.lnote.de.3"/> (vor <hi rend="italic">A</hi>) Aller Heiligenfest<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#ICn_12.lnote.de.4"/> [1. Nov.] ebenso viel (und wiederum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#ICn_12.lnote.de.5"/> zu Mariae Reinigung<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#ICn_12.lnote.de.6"/> [2. Febr. Vorabend] ebenso viel. <hi rend="italic">Ld Versionen</hi>)</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">And light-dues three times a year: half a penny's worth of wax from every hide, first on Easter Eve and again at (before, A) All Saints [1 November] as much (and again at the Purification of Mary [eve of 2 February] as much, Ld and the Latin versions).</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-g-a"><ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#ICn_12.robnote.n.1"/><pb n="165" ed="#robertson"/>And light dues [shall be paid] three times a year: first a halfpennyworth of wax from every hide on Easter Eve, and as much afterwards at the feast of All Saints, [and as much afterwards at the Feast of the Purification of St Mary]<ptr type="editorNote" n="2" target="#ICn_12.robnote.n.2"/>.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="245" ed="#rabin-doml"/>And the dues for the lighting of the church are to be paid three times a year: first, a halfpennyworth of wax from each hide on the eve of Easter, and just as much afterward on the Feast of All Saints, and an equal amount again at the Feast of the Purification of Saint Mary.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="295"><ref target="clause:VIAtr_19">VI Atr 19</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">Vgl. VI Atr. 19</note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="356"><label>loose/partial source (in parentheses)</label> <ref target="clause:VIAtr_19">VI Atr 19</ref> <quote>Table 5.4, I Cn 12: (HomN XXIII, LXI) Cn 1018 13:5 (II Can Eg 54  VIII Atr 12:1, VI Atr 19)</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="356"><label>loose/partial source (in parentheses)</label> <ref target="clause:VIIIAtr_12-1">VIII Atr 12.1</ref> <quote>Table 5.4, I Cn 12: (HomN XXIII, LXI) Cn 1018 13:5 (II Can Eg 54  VIII Atr 12:1, VI Atr 19)</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="356"><label>source (roman)</label> <ref target="clause:Cn-1018_part-035">Cn 1018 13.5</ref> <quote>Table 5.4, I Cn 12: (HomN XXIII, LXI) Cn 1018 13:5 (II Can Eg 54  VIII Atr 12:1, VI Atr 19)</quote></note>
        <note type="editorial">The bracketed third payment was added in the margin of G in the 16th century from Ld (Liebermann would supply ‘æfene’ after ‘þæm’). Liebermann compares VI Atr 19.; BR: added from Gesetze I p. 295, October 2026 (MS Cons)</note>
        <note type="textual" source="#rabin-doml">eft on: eft to A</note>
        <note type="textual" source="#rabin-doml">and eft to þæm æfene sanctan Marian clænsunge ealswa: omitted G (likely by scribal error), but added in a sixteenth-century hand</note>
        <note type="translator" source="#rabin-doml">Feast of the Purification of Saint Mary: February 2. The feast is sometimes also referred to as Candlemas; compare Canons 54.</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_12.lnote.oe.9" n="9" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">294</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-ra <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-ra Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_12.lnote.oe.10" n="10" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">294</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-ing. <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-ing. Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_12.lnote.oe.11" n="11" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">294</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-cer <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-cer Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_12.lnote.oe.12" n="12" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">294</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">to <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">to Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_12.lnote.oe.13" n="13" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">294</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">ealswa micel <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">ealswa micel Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_12.lnote.oe.star2" n="**" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">294</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">⁊ — ealswa <hi rend="italic">aus Ld im</hi> 16. <hi rend="italic">Jh. am Rande G</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">⁊ — ealswa from Ld, in the 16th cent., in the margin G</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_12.lnote.oe.14" n="14" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">294</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">ergänze</hi> æfene</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">supply æfene</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_12.lnote.oe.6" n="6" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">294</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt R</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in R</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_12.lnote.oe.7" n="7" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">294</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">obul. <hi rend="italic">K</hi>; obl. <hi rend="italic">Dm</hi>; -te <hi rend="italic">R</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">obul. K; obl. Dm; -te R</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_12.lnote.oe.8" n="8" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">294</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt KR Hk; übergeschrieben in derselben Hand Dm T</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">missing in KR Hk; written above in the same hand Dm T</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_12.lnote.oe.9-2" n="9" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">294</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt K</hi>; t. t. <hi rend="italic">fehlt R</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">missing in K; t. t. missing in R</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_12.lnote.oe.11-2" n="11" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">295</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">hinter II Eg.</hi> 4, 3</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">after II Eg. 4, 3</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_12.lnote.oe.12-2" n="12" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">295</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">l. ter <hi rend="italic">als ein Wort Cb</hi>; lithig. <hi rend="italic">Lb Jo</hi>; lichtinges. <hi rend="italic">S</hi>; lihtscot <hi rend="italic">Di</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">l. ter as one word Cb; lithig. Lb Jo; lichtinges. S; lihtscot Di</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_12.lnote.oe.13-2" n="13" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">295</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">nur Cb</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">only Cb</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_12.lnote.oe.14-2" n="14" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">295</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt Di Lb S</hi>; <hi rend="italic">übergeschr. H</hi>; sulinghida <hi rend="italic">Cb</hi>; sulinghyda <hi rend="italic">T</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">missing in Di Lb S; written above H; sulinghida Cb; sulinghyda T</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_12.lnote.oe.15" n="15" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">295</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">in m. A. [<hi rend="italic">falsch</hi>] <hi rend="italic">fehlt Di</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">in m. A. [wrong] missing in Di</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_12.lnote.oe.16" n="16" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">295</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">et <hi rend="italic">fügt zu S</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">et added by S</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="ICn_12.lnote.oe.17" n="17" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">295</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">folgt I</hi> 11</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">followed by I 11</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="ICn_12.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">200</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Hufe 1k. 3; Lichtschoss 2—3</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Hufe 1k. 3; Lichtschoss 2—3</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="ICn_12.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">200</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Hufe 1k. 3; Lichtschoss 2—3</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Hufe 1k. 3; Lichtschoss 2—3</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="ICn_12.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">200</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">‘Vorabend’ Inst, wohl richtig, da so in Eadgar-Glosse ed. Thorpe <hi rend="italic">Anc. laws</hi> 400</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">‘eve’ Inst, probably correctly, since so in an Eadgar gloss ed. Thorpe <hi rend="italic">Anc. laws</hi> 400</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="ICn_12.lnote.de.4" n="4" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">200</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Dafür ‘Weihnachten’ <hi rend="italic">Hom. n</hi>. Wulfstan 311</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Instead ‘Christmas’ <hi rend="italic">Hom. n</hi>. Wulfstan 311</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="ICn_12.lnote.de.5" n="5" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">200</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Auslassung in G und A, durch Gleichheit des Zeilenendes <hi rend="italic">ealswa</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Omission in G and A, owing to the identical line-ending <hi rend="italic">ealswa</hi></seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="ICn_12.lnote.de.6" n="6" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">200</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Mariä (<hi rend="italic">s. d. Gl</hi> 3a. 4) Himmelfahrt wohl nur Irrtum in Inst</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">The Assumption of Mary (<hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word in <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> 3a. 4) is probably only an error in Inst</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="ICn_12.robnote.n.1" n="1" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">349</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">With caps. 12–14, 1 cf. VI Atr. 19–22.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="ICn_12.robnote.n.2" n="2" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">349</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Liebermann suggests that the last part of the clause, which is found in Ld, Q, Inst. and Cons., may have been missed in G and A because of the repetition of <hi rend="italic">ealswa</hi>.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="ICn_12.robnote.fn.9" n="9" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">164</biblScope></bibl><label>on</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">to</hi> A, Ld.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="ICn_12.robnote.fn.10" n="10" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">164</biblScope></bibl><label>eft</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">⁊ <hi rend="italic">eft…ealswa</hi> Ld and in the margin of G in handwriting of 16th cent.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="ICn_12.robnote.fn.11" n="11" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">164</biblScope></bibl><label>æfene</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Following Liebermann.</seg></note>
